{
  html: "<html><head></head><body><p>Role Title: Military/Veteran Mental Health Experts</p><p><br></p><p>Role Type: Contractor</p><p><br></p><p>Location: Remote</p><p><br></p><p>micro1 is engaging Mental Health Experts to contribute to a high-impact customer project focused on the advancement of AI technologies in mental health. In this role, you'll apply your expertise to help train next-generation AI systems. Your work will shape how models learn, reason, and perform through high-quality, real-world input. No prior experience in AI is required — your domain knowledge is what matters. </p><p><br></p><p>This opportunity is ideal for professionals with substantial experience in providing direct patient care to military personnel or veterans, whether as board-certified psychiatrists (post-residency) or clinical psychologists (PhD completed). </p><p><br></p><p>Scope of Work</p><ol><li>Review and evaluate mental health materials, case studies, and simulated patient interactions relevant to military and veteran populations.</li><li>Provide expert feedback and nuanced analysis to refine AI models' understanding of clinical best practices, diagnostic processes, and therapeutic approaches.</li><li>Create, edit, and curate prompts, responses, and scenarios that reflect real-world challenges experienced by military and veteran patients.</li><li>Identify domain-specific terminology, cultural nuances, and communication techniques essential for effective mental health support in this population.</li><li>Participate in virtual discussions or consultative sessions to align on project goals and share clinical perspectives.</li><li>Document findings, recommendations, and potential improvements in a clear, structured, and accessible format.</li><li>Ensure all contributions meet high standards for clinical accuracy, relevance, and sensitivity to the unique needs of service members and veterans.</li></ol><p><br></p><p>Preferred Qualifications</p><ol><li>Medical doctor (psychiatrist) with completed residency, or psychologist with completed PhD.</li><li>Demonstrated direct patient care experience with military and/or veteran populations.</li><li>Deep familiarity with trauma, PTSD, TBI, adjustment disorders, and other conditions prevalent among service members.</li><li>Outstanding written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to translate complex clinical concepts for diverse audiences.</li><li>Experience developing or reviewing clinical content, training materials, or assessment tools.</li><li>Strong attention to detail, clinical accuracy, and cultural competence.</li><li>Adaptability and interest in contributing to technology-driven mental health solutions.</li><li><span>We are prioritizing applicants with proficiency in one or more of these languages:</span><em> Japanese, French, Tagalog, Malay, Lithuanian, Russian, Georgian, Polish, Marathi, Bengali, Urdu, Vietnamese, Swahili, Mandarin, Cantonese, Indonesian, Turkish, Gujarati, Bulgarian.</em></li></ol></body></html>",
