  html: "<html><head></head><body><p>Role Title: Child Development Psychologist (PhD)</p><p><br></p><p>Role Type: Contractor</p><p><br></p><p>Location: Remote</p><p><br></p><p>micro1 is engaging Psychologists to contribute their expertise to a customer's project at the intersection of psychology and technology. In this role, you'll apply your expertise to help train next-generation AI systems. Your work will shape how models learn, reason, and perform through high-quality, real-world input. No prior experience in AI is required — your domain knowledge is what matters. This opportunity is especially suited for contributors who have a background in research or academic work related to child development or developmental psychology, with or without direct clinical experience.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Scope of Work</p><ol><li>Evaluate, review, and annotate data sets relevant to child development and developmental psychology for AI system training.</li><li>Provide detailed insights and feedback on the accuracy, cultural appropriateness, and developmental relevance of data and model outputs.</li><li>Contribute expert analysis to scenario development, test cases, and real-world situations involving children’s learning and behavior.</li><li>Collaborate with interdisciplinary teams to inform model improvements and ensure psychological integrity in AI interactions.</li><li>Create or refine guidelines for AI systems to better address linguistic, cognitive, and psychosocial aspects of child development across diverse backgrounds.</li><li>Document findings and recommendations with clarity and depth to support ongoing AI research and development.</li></ol><p><br></p><p>Preferred Qualifications</p><ol><li>Doctorate (PhD) in Child Development, Developmental Psychology, or closely related field.</li><li>Demonstrated involvement in technology-driven, digital, or AI-focused projects relevant to child development is highly desirable.</li><li>Comfortable working remotely on digital pl