{
  html: "<html><head></head><body><p>Role Title: Autodesk Fusion 360 Specialist</p><p><br></p><p>Role Type: Contractor</p><p><br></p><p>Location: Remote</p><p><br></p><p>micro1 is engaging Autodesk Fusion 360 Specialists to contribute expertise on a high-impact customer project focused on advanced parametric CAD modeling. In this role, you'll apply your expertise to help train next-generation AI systems. Your work will shape how models learn, reason, and perform through high-quality, real-world input. No prior experience in AI is required — your domain knowledge is what matters.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Note on Software:</strong> We're looking for experts with strong 3D parametric CAD modelling experience — for example, in Autodesk Fusion 360 Specialist. This experience is directly transferable to FreeCAD, which is the software this project will focus on. Prior FreeCAD experience is ideal.</p><p><br></p><p>Scope of Work</p><ol><li>Develop fully parametric 3D models of mechanical parts and assemblies based on detailed written briefs, emphasizing robust sketching, constraints, and feature trees.</li><li>Edit and update existing parametric CAD models to reflect evolving requirements, ensuring manufacturability and compliance with specifications.</li><li>Audit and review CAD models for dimensional accuracy, tolerance application, and alignment with design intent, calling out any gaps or deviations.</li><li>Support AI model training by delivering consistent, high-quality CAD data and clear documentation of design decisions.</li><li>Apply deep working knowledge of manufacturing processes—such as injection molding, sheet metal fabrication, CNC machining, and casting/forging—to optimize designs for production.</li><li>Communicate design rationale, feedback, and technical insights with clarity—both in writing and verbally—in support of collaboration and continuous project improvement.</li></ol><p><br></p><p>Preferred Qualifications</p><ol><li>Extensive hands-on experience with parametric CAD platforms (ideally FreeCAD, with strong proficiency in Autodesk Fusion 360, SolidWorks, or Inventor acceptable).</li><li>Proven application of GD&amp;T principles (ASME Y14.5 or equivalent) in real-world projects.</li><li>Demonstrated DFM expertise across at least 2-3 manufacturing processes relevant to the project scope.</li><li>4+ years of applied experience for model editing tasks; 10+ years for complex model creation assignments.</li><li>Proven ability to tackle assembly-level modeling, not just single-part tasks.</li><li>Experience in reverse engineering workflows, such as scan-to-CAD or point cloud conversions, is highly valued.</li><li>Familiarity with CAD automation or scripting (e.g., Python, iLogic, NX Open, VBA) considered a strong plus for automating and standardizing workflows.</li></ol></body></html>",
