[MICRO1] Processing 79/331: Retail CX & Policy Specialist 
{
  html: '<html><head></head><body><p>Role Title: Retail CX &amp; Policy Specialist</p><p><br></p><p>Role Type: Contractor</p><p><br></p><p>Location: Remote, US or Canada-based.</p><p><br></p><p>micro1 is engaging Retail CX Policy Experts to contribute to a customer’s project focused on defining ground-truth operational guidelines for AI-powered customer experience (CX) systems. In this role, you’ll apply your expertise to help train next-generation AI systems. Your work will shape how models learn, reason, and perform through high-quality, real-world input. No prior experience in AI is required — your domain knowledge is what matters.</p><p><br></p><p>You will author authentic return, refund, and eligibility policies modeled after real-world US retail and e-commerce operations, creating the authoritative standards by which AI agents are evaluated. This opportunity involves comprehensive policy creation and scenario design, ensuring the coverage of nuanced, edge-case situations encountered in modern CX environments.</p><p><br></p><p>Scope of Work</p><p><br></p><ol><li>Author and document detailed return, refund, and eligibility policies reflecting up-to-date US retail and e-commerce practices.</li><li>Design nuanced customer-service scenarios, including edge cases, to surface policy ambiguities and operational gaps.</li><li>Establish clear, correct customer-service resolutions for both standard and exceptional situations according to your authored policies.</li><li>Create precise grading rubrics for evaluating agent performance on complex, multi-step customer experience cases.</li><li>Identify, document, and escalate policy conflicts or ambiguities to ensure comprehensive AI environment coverage.</li><li>Collaborate with domain leads and quality calibration contributors to evolve policies as project requirements shift.</li><li>Define and validate “golden outcomes” for AI model training and assessment.</li></ol><p><br></p><p>Preferred Qualifications</p><p><br></p><ol><li>3–5+ years of hands-on experience in US retail or e-commerce CX operations, including escalation handling and process design.</li><li>Direct background in authoring or redesigning return, refund, and eligibility policies (not just executing prewritten guidelines).</li><li>Deep knowledge of US retail conventions: return windows, restocking fees, gift returns, damaged goods, chargeback handling, and marketplace fulfillment.</li><li>Exceptional written and verbal communication skills, with a focus on unambiguous policy documentation.</li><li>Bachelor’s degree preferred (business, operations, or related disciplines) or equivalent real-world expertise.</li><li>Experience across multiple retail categories (such as apparel, electronics, home goods, and third-party marketplaces) is a plus.</li><li>Previous involvement in CX process design, knowledge management, or contract-based AI evaluation projects is advantageous.</li></ol><p><br></p><p>Start Timeline &amp; Availability</p><p>We typically fill roles within <strong>48 hours</strong> and are looking for experts ready to jump in right away. If selected, we expect you to start your first tasks within 24–48 hours of completing onboarding.</p></body></html>',
