{
  html: "<html><head></head><body><p>Role Title: Tax Advisor (CPA)</p><p><br></p><p>Role Type: Contractor (Part Time)</p><p><br></p><p>Location: Remote (US Only)</p><p><br></p><p>micro1 is engaging Tax Advising Experts to contribute to a customer's project focused on tax preparation and advisory services. In this role, you'll apply your expertise to help train next-generation AI systems. Your work will shape how models learn, reason, and perform through high-quality, real-world input. No prior experience in AI is required — your domain knowledge is what matters.</p><p><strong>Scope of Work</strong></p><ol><li>Prepare and review personal (Form 1040) and small business (Schedule C, S-Corp 1120-S, Partnership 1065) income tax returns to ensure accuracy and compliance with current tax laws.</li><li>Advise on tax optimization strategies and clarify complex tax concepts in clear written and verbal communication for clients.</li><li>Assess and critique AI-generated tax advice or content against provided rubrics, delivering concise written feedback to drive model improvement.</li><li>Verify documentation and support clients with questions regarding tax filing status, deadlines, and required forms.</li><li>Contribute to the development and refinement of evaluation rubrics and grading criteria for tax-related outputs.</li><li>Stay up to date with changes in federal and state tax codes relevant to client cases and project deliverables.</li></ol><p><strong>Required Qualifications</strong></p><ol><li>Active CPA license in good standing, with eligibility to practice in the United States.</li><li>Extensive experience in preparing and filing both personal and small business tax returns.</li><li>Proficiency in current federal tax regulations and at least one state's income tax requirements.</li><li>Exceptional written and verbal communication skills, with a strong ability to translate technical tax topics for diverse audiences.</li><li>5+ years of professional tax preparation/adviso