{
  html: "<html><head></head><body><p>Role Title: Senior DoD Staff Writing SME</p><p><br></p><p>Role Type: Contractor</p><p><br></p><p>Location: Remote (US Only) </p><p><br></p><p>micro1 is engaging Senior DoD Staff Writing SMEs to contribute expert knowledge and writing skills to a pivotal customer project. In this role, you'll apply your expertise to help train next-generation AI systems. Your work will shape how models learn, reason, and perform through high-quality, real-world input. No prior experience in AI is required — your domain knowledge is what matters.</p><p><br></p><p>Scope of Work</p><ol><li>Develop and provide well-structured prompts, input artifacts, and golden responses for diverse Department of Defense (DoD) staff writing tasks such as WARs, SITREPs, executive summaries, and performance reports.</li><li>Create grading guidelines to evaluate and score AI-generated outputs, ensuring alignment with DoD standards and expectations for accuracy, tone, and compliance.</li><li>Produce authentic report artifacts reflecting the style, structure, and language used in real-world DoD documentation across a range of operational and administrative scenarios.</li><li>Contribute to the design and review of test materials that evaluate AI capabilities in summarizing and reporting tasks typically performed by federal personnel.</li><li>Engage in feedback cycles to refine prompts, responses, and grading rubrics based on project needs and model performance.</li><li>Leverage back-office and communication experience to simulate weekly, monthly, and ad hoc reporting formats familiar to federal organizations.</li></ol><p><br></p><p>Preferred Qualifications</p><ol><li>Former federal contributor for the U.S. Department of War (Department of Defense), with at least 3 years of relevant experience.</li><li>Experience producing key reporting artifacts such as Weekly Activity Reports (WARs), Situation Reports (SITREPs), executive summaries, and similar standard formats.</li><li>Background in one of the six branches of the U.S. military, with diversity of experience across different roles and units preferred.</li><li>Demonstrated excellence in written and verbal communication, with clear attention to detail and audience-appropriate language.</li><li>Familiarity with back-office tools and processes, including the production and formatting of PowerPoint briefings, memos, Excel summaries, and related documentation.</li><li>Strong analytical skills for evaluating and providing constructive feedback on AI-generated staff writing outputs.</li><li>US-based with an understanding of federal compliance, reporting requirements, and DoD-specific terminology and workflows.</li></ol></body></html>",
