 and effective communication channels.</li></ol><p><br></p><p>Preferred Qualifications</p><ol><li>Extensive hands-on experience in simulation and CAE-heavy mechanical engineering assignments.</li><li>Proven proficiency with Codex, Claude Science, Claude Code, and Claude Cowork as coding sequence generators in technical scenarios.</li><li>Demonstrated ability to apply AI agents to sophisticated engineering challenges—including navigating ambiguous requirements, large-scale debugging, or architectural overhauls.</li><li>Exceptional written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to translate complex technical workflows into concise documentation and feedback.</li><li>Active involvement in current STEM fields, using AI agentics as a practical extension of real-world engineering problem-solving.</li><li>Experience documenting technical workflows and providing actionable insights for technology improvement or training purposes.</li><li>Familiarity with the broader landscape of AI-driven engineering tools and a track record of experimentation and adaptation to new technologies.</li></ol></body></html>",
