[MICRO1] Processing 140/331: CNC Machinist
{
  html: "<html><head></head><body><p>Role Title: CNC Machinist</p><p><br></p><p>Role Type: Contractor</p><p><br></p><p>Location: Remote</p><p><br></p><p>micro1 is engaging CNC Machinists to contribute expertise to a customer’s project focused on advanced part production and process optimization. In this role, you'll apply your expertise to help train next-generation AI systems. Your work will shape how models learn, reason, and perform through high-quality, real-world input. No prior experience in AI is required — your domain knowledge is what matters. This engagement centers on operating and setting up both hobbyist (e.g., Makera Carvera) and industrial (e.g., Haas VF-2) CNC machines, interpreting engineering documentation, and troubleshooting across a range of materials and geometries. Contributors will provide input on machining processes, best practices, and issue resolution, ensuring high standards of quality and consistency throughout the project.</p><p><br></p><p>Scope of Work</p><ol><li>Set up and operate CNC machines across multiple platforms, including desktop and industrial models</li><li>Load and verify CNC programs, install tooling, configure work-holding, and set work offsets for various projects</li><li>Run first-piece cycles, inspect machined parts against drawings, and adjust setups to ensure dimensional accuracy</li><li>Perform routine machine maintenance and diagnose issues such as tool wear, chatter, or dimensional drift</li><li>Utilize precision measurement instruments (calipers, micrometers, indicators, CMM) to validate parts and ensure compliance with specifications</li><li>Interpret engineering drawings, GD&amp;T callouts, and manufacturing documentation to guide part production</li><li>Collaborate and provide feedback to CAM programmers and other stakeholders on setup optimization and manufacturability</li></ol><p><br></p><p>Preferred Qualifications</p><ol><li>5+ years of hands-on CNC machining experience, including both setup and production</li><li>Expertise operating Haas control systems (VF-2 or similar platforms) required</li><li>Familiarity with hobbyist/desktop CNC platforms (such as Makera Carvera) strongly preferred</li><li>Proven proficiency in blueprint reading, GD&amp;T interpretation, and use of advanced measurement tools</li><li>Experience working with a range of materials, including both metals and plastics</li><li>Outstanding written and verbal English communication skills for clear documentation and feedback</li><li>Demonstrated ability to troubleshoot machining processes, optimize setups, and maintain a safe, organized workspace</li></ol></body></html>",
