[MICRO1] Processing 190/331: Mechanical Design / CAD Expert 
{
  html: "<html><head></head><body><p>Job Description Role Title: CAD / Mechanical Design Expert</p><p>Role Type: Contractor</p><p>Location: Remote</p><p><br></p><p>micro1 is selecting CAD / Mechanical Design Experts to contribute to a customer's project focused on advancing the capabilities of AI technologies in mechanical design engineering. In this role, you'll apply your expertise to help train next-generation AI systems. Your work will shape how models learn, reason, and perform through high-quality, real-world input. No prior experience in AI is required, your domain knowledge is what matters. This is an opportunity to impact the future of engineering by ensuring that AI systems can accurately interpret, solve, and explain complex mechanical design challenges spanning GD&amp;T, tolerance stack-up, DFM, and drawing release. Experts with a passion for precision, technical detail, and clear written and verbal communication will find this engagement both rewarding and influential.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Scope of Work</strong></p><ol><li>Evaluate and solve advanced mechanical design and CAD problems spanning part/assembly design, GD&amp;T, tolerance stack-up, and DFM.</li><li>Review and assess AI-generated technical responses for technical correctness, accuracy, and engineering quality.</li><li>Apply practical engineering judgment to real-world production design scenarios and theoretical questions.</li><li>Analyze and troubleshoot mechanical design problems using industry-standard techniques such as tolerance stack-up analysis, GD&amp;T per ASME Y14.5, and design-for-manufacturability/assembly review.</li><li>Contribute domain expertise to inform model improvements and refine AI reasoning in mechanical design and CAD.</li><li>Document feedback and provide clear written and verbal explanations to enhance AI learning and performance.</li><li>Collaborate remotely with a distributed team of experts and project participants.</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong>Preferred Qualifications</strong></p><ol><li>MS or BS in Mechanical Engineering, Aerospace, or Industrial Design (CSWP/CSWE a plus).</li><li>At least 5 years of experience in production design roles, having personally owned designs through GD&amp;T, tolerance stacks, DFM, and drawing release.</li><li>Expert knowledge of parametric CAD modeling, GD&amp;T per ASME Y14.5, tolerance stack-up analysis, and design-for-manufacturability/assembly principles.</li><li>Proven ability to take a design from concept through detail drawings, ECR/ECN, and production release.</li><li>Familiarity with relevant standards bodies (ASME Y14.5, ASME B89 dimensional metrology) and manufacturing process constraints (machining, sheet metal, injection molding, casting).</li><li>Professional English proficiency with exceptional written and verbal communication skills.</li><li>Experience with CAD platforms (SolidWorks, Creo, NX, CATIA, Inventor), PLM/PDM systems, or CAM/CNC programming is a plus.</li><li>Strongly preferred — evidence of problem-authoring rigor, such as: service on an olympiad problem committee; a textbook problem-set or solutions-manual author credit; an item-writer role on an NCEES or academic qualifying-exam committee; service on an ASME Y14.5, ASME B89, or related dimensioning/tolerancing standards committee; a top placement or team-lead role in Formula SAE/Formula Student, ASME Student Design Competition/HPVC, MATE ROV, or a DARPA challenge; or an early-career fellowship/grant (NSF CAREER, DOE Early Career, Sloan Fellowship) or ASME Fellow recognition.</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong>Compensation Structure</strong></p><p><span>Compensation is output-based; experts are paid per task that meets the project specifications. The time required to complete work may vary depending on the expert’s experience and workflow. Minimum submission requirements apply. Experts must submit a minimum of tasks per week.</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Start Timeline &amp; Availability</strong></p><p><span>We typically fill roles within </span><strong>48 hours</strong><span> and are looking for experts ready to jump in right away. If selected, we expect you to start your first tasks within 24–48 hours of completing onboarding.</span></p></body></html>",
