{
  html: "<html><head></head><body><p>Role Title: Corporate Attorney (US based)</p><p><br></p><p>Role Type: Contractor</p><p><br></p><p>Location: Remote</p><p><br></p><p>micro1 is engaging Corporate Lawyers (US based) to contribute their legal expertise to a customer's project focused on commercial, contract, corporate, M&amp;A, and general counsel matters. In this role, you'll apply your expertise to help train next-generation AI systems. Your work will shape how models learn, reason, and perform through high-quality, real-world input. No prior experience in AI is required — your domain knowledge is what matters.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Scope of Work</strong></p><ol><li>Evaluate and analyze a wide range of corporate, commercial, and M&amp;A documents for accuracy, enforceability, and compliance with US law.</li><li>Draft, review, and provide feedback on contracts, policies, and agreements reflecting best practices in corporate law.</li><li>Translate complex legal concepts into clear, accessible explanations for use in AI system development.</li><li>Identify and summarize key legal issues, trends, and risk areas in business transactions and contract negotiations.</li><li>Contribute real-world legal scenarios, case studies, and document samples to enhance AI training datasets.</li><li>Collaborate asynchronously with project stakeholders to clarify deliverables and address questions related to corporate law topics.</li><li>Deliver precise written and verbal insights, ensuring nuanced understanding of legal language and its practical applications.</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong>Preferred Qualifications</strong></p><ol><li>Juris Doctor (JD) from an accredited US law school and active bar membership in at least one US jurisdiction.</li><li>Minimum 5 years of experience in corporate, business, or transactional law, including exposure to M&amp;A, contracts, and risk management.</li><li>Demonstrated experience as outside counsel, in-house corporate counsel, or as a legal consultant to business clients.</li><li>Exceptional written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to distill complex legal issues for diverse audiences.</li><li>Familiarity with the US legal landscape, including commercial and regulatory compliance requirements.</li><li>Proficiency in reviewing and drafting a variety of corporate and commercial agreements.</li><li>Intellectual curiosity and eagerness to contribute to innovative technology-driven projects.</li></ol></body></html>",
