  html: "<html><head></head><body><p>Role Title: Content Editor.</p><p><br></p><p>Role Type: Contractor.</p><p><br></p><p>Location: Remote</p><p><br></p><p>micro1 is looking for an experienced <strong>Video Editor</strong> to support our internal marketing and content initiatives on a project basis. You'll be responsible for creating engaging, high-performing video content across multiple social media platforms, helping grow the micro1 brand through compelling storytelling and modern editing techniques.</p><p>This opportunity is focused on professionals with strong portfolios editing content for platforms such as <strong>YouTube, X (Twitter), LinkedIn, YouTube Shorts, Instagram Reels, and TikTok</strong>. The primary focus is on <strong>horizontal (16:9)</strong> content for YouTube, X, and LinkedIn, while experience with <strong>vertical (9:16)</strong> content is also valued. We're looking for editors with proven expertise in fast-paced editing, motion graphics, dynamic captions, sound design, and social-first editing techniques that maximize viewer retention and engagement.</p><p><br></p><h3>Scope of Work</h3><ol><li>Edit and enhance video content for micro1's social media channels, with an emphasis on horizontal (16:9) content for YouTube, X (Twitter), and LinkedIn.</li><li>Create compelling hooks, dynamic captions, motion graphics, and engaging visual elements that capture attention and increase watch time.</li><li>Incorporate B-roll, sound effects, transitions, speed ramps, zooms, punch-ins, and text animations where appropriate.</li><li>Optimize pacing, music, and audio to produce polished, high-retention content aligned with current social media trends.</li><li>Deliver high-quality final assets while meeting project deadlines and maintaining brand consistency.</li><li>Collaborate remotely with the marketing team to understand creative direction, iterate on feedback, and execute content that aligns with campaign objectives.</li><li>Maintain organized project files and deliverables throughout the editing process.</li></ol><h3>Preferred Qualifications</h3><ol><li>Portfolio showcasing high-quality editing for <strong>YouTube, X (Twitter), LinkedIn</strong>, and/or short-form platforms such as <strong>Instagram Reels, TikTok, or YouTube Shorts</strong>.</li><li>Experience as a <strong>Social Media Video Editor, Short-form Video Editor, YouTube Video Editor, Reels/TikTok Editor, Content Editor,</strong> or <strong>Content Creator/Video Editor</strong>.</li><li>Previous work with <strong>YouTubers, personal brands, coaches, SaaS startups, marketing agencies, B2B companies,</strong> or <strong>podcasts</strong>.</li><li>Advanced proficiency in <strong>Adobe Premiere Pro, DaVinci Resolve, Final Cut Pro</strong>, or similar professional editing software. Experience with motion graphics is a strong plus.</li><li>Strong communication skills and the ability to interpret creative briefs, incorporate feedback, and work independently in a remote environment.</li><li>Demonstrated ability to produce engaging content using strong hooks, dynamic captions, jump cuts, graphic overlays, text animations, sound design, and other techniques that improve audience retention.</li><li>A strong understanding of current social media trends, platform-specific best practices, and content optimized for engagement.</li></ol><p><br></p></body></html>",
