{
  html: "<html><head></head><body><p>Role Title: Korean Transcription Expert</p><p><br></p><p>Role Type: Contractor</p><p><br></p><p>Location: Remote</p><p><br></p><p>micro1 is engaging Korean Transcription Experts to contribute to a high-impact project for an innovative customer. In this role, you'll apply your expertise to help train next-generation AI systems. Your work will shape how models learn, reason, and perform through high-quality, real-world input. No prior experience in AI is required — your domain knowledge is what matters.</p><p><br></p><p>Scope of Work</p><ol><li>Transcribe audio samples accurately and consistently, ensuring precision in capturing both Korean and English content.</li><li>Review, edit, and proofread transcriptions for quality assurance, correcting errors and verifying linguistic accuracy.</li><li>Annotate audio files with relevant metadata and contextual notes to support AI training requirements.</li><li>Collaborate with project coordinators to clarify guidelines and maintain alignment with evolving project specifications.</li><li>Deliver completed transcription assignments within established project timelines and quality benchmarks.</li><li>Contribute feedback on workflow processes, tool usability, and linguistic challenges encountered during transcription tasks.</li></ol><p><br></p><p>Preferred Qualifications</p><ol><li>Native or near-native fluency in Korean, with advanced comprehension of both spoken and written language.</li><li>Professional experience performing audio transcription, especially in settings where high accuracy is essential.</li><li>Demonstrated attention to detail and strong commitment to delivering error-free language data.</li><li>Familiarity with industry-standard transcription tools or platforms.</li><li>Proficiency in both written and verbal communication, with the ability to articulate guidance, clarify ambiguities, and document findings.</li><li>Ability to manage multiple assignments and adapt to changing project requirements.</li><li>Prior experience with projects involving AI training, data annotation, or language resource development is a plus.</li></ol></body></html>",
